<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 14 March, from 1757 to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1757 CE <span class="tih-ago">269 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Admiral John Byng executed by firing squad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Convicted of failing to do his utmost to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Minorca</a>, Byng was shot on the deck of HMS Monarch at Portsmouth. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voltaire">Voltaire</a> mocked the English for killing an admiral 'to encourage the others'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/eli-whitney" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eli-whitney.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1794 CE <span class="tih-ago">232 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Eli Whitney patents the cotton gin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Whitney's machine separated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> fibre from seeds far faster than by hand. It made short-staple cotton highly profitable and fuelled a vast expansion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-south">American South</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-south">American South</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1879 CE <span class="tih-ago">147 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albert Einstein is born in Ulm</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Einstein's theories of special and general relativity transformed ideas of space, time and gravity. He won the 1921 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> for explaining the photoelectric effect.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1900 CE <span class="tih-ago">126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gold Standard Act puts the dollar on gold</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President McKinley signed the act fixing the dollar's value in gold and ending the long political fight over free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>. The US left the gold standard domestically in 1933.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1942 CE <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Penicillin saves its first American patient</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Anne Miller, dying of streptococcal blood poisoning after a miscarriage, was treated at a New Haven hospital with a scarce supply of penicillin. She recovered and lived to the age of 90.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1964 CE <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jack Ruby convicted of murdering Lee Harvey Oswald</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Dallas jury found the nightclub owner guilty of shooting Kennedy's accused assassin on live television and sentenced him to death. The verdict was overturned, and Ruby died before a retrial.</p></div></li></ol>
